 "biomes": {
  "SUBJECTS_liquid_connections": {
   "label": "Liquid connections: pump, hose, joins",
   "slug": "liquid_connections",
   "subjects": true,
   "ground_terrain": "Soil",
   "title": "Liquid connections: pump, hose, joins \u2014 game art",
   "lead_html": "<p>Owner 2026-10-16: <i>\u201cthe flexible hose seems absolutely enormous when attached to things like pumps \u2026 The pump needs to be made to be commensurate with such a thick tube. And we might need to shrink the tube diameter a bit \u2026 anything the hoses can connect to (pumps, tanks, reels) as well as when you place a tank, reel, or pump next to each other some kind of connection should be visually apparent \u2026 The pipe needs connectors that show where it's connecting.\u201d</i></p><p><b>Numbers.</b> Hose today: 0.38 cell flat / 0.465 plump. Rigid pipe: 0.23. Pump today: 1 x 1 cell. <b>Proposed:</b> hose 0.65x = <b>0.25 flat / 0.30 plump</b> (still a little thicker than the pipe); pump <b>footprint 2 x 1, drawn 2 x 2</b> (about 1.9 x 1.1 cells of machine), its two port flanges sized to the 0.30 hose.</p><p><b>Rows.</b> Pump, flange and saddle, one row per look (A = the only candidate; pick it, or note what to change). Then one mockup per join type, each column a look: <b>top half today, bottom half proposed</b> (pipe arm running to the tank or pump edge plus a flange; a flange pair where a pump or reel touches a tank; a saddle where a hose couples onto a pipe). Nothing is installed; the hose stays at today's width and the fittings stay switched off until you rule. Design note: design/RimMandrake/liquid_connections_visuals_2026-10-16.md.</p>",
   "rows": [
